e it now very good for luxury  tourism  um but also the question i think that we  at first had was you know  why  well why are people no longer  quarantined here why is quarantine not  happening where does quarantine occur um  is quarantine you know something that is  obsolete and part of the past and  something that we've moved past  and don't no longer need to do and so i  think that we began looking this at this  question somewhat embarrassingly as you  know what was quarantine um you know  what happened to it and i think that the  minute you start looking into it uh as  happened with us you start realizing  that quarantine it's not that it's this  niche thing that you can't find anywhere  in fact it's everywhere you know it's in  the food supply it's in  astronauts going back and forth to the  international space station it's in our  metaphors it's in our mythology  you know it is in our architectural  history it's a whole um you know  neighborhoods you know you can actually  still see it on maps today like there's  a quarantine  um  what is the name of the road in  baltimore that now has a landfill on it  quarantine road  but so you can even see it in the in the  names of rode the lazarettos and  quarantines and these things pop up and  so i guess it sort of became this thing  where we started pulling on the string  of quarantine um and we did that  exhibition and then a couple years went  by i worked on a different book project  and nikki has a different book project  and then just decided that we just  couldn't stop thinking about quarantine  we still kept seeing it everywhere and  we thought you know what we should  return to this and and actually write a  book that ironically was going to be  called the coming quarantine and and  there was not a book about quarantine  there were books about specific  pandemics and specific quarantines and  responses to those pandemics but there  was nothing that looked at quarantine  across the span of history and across  all of its different contexts and we  felt that it had this really interesting  and powerful logic to it  that you could only pull out by looking  at it at it  across all of those contexts and so we  wanted to do that  nice and what's uh what's next for you  next for me is the book that i was  supposed to be writing instead of the  quarantine  jeff referred to my book project i'm i'm  writing a book about refrigeration which  i spoke about at the interval um and  which will um it's moving very slowly  because things move slowly in the cold  but it will one day be finished  how about you jeff and uh i guess for me  a whole bunch of little things at the  moment uh so some short fiction uh i  have a grant for some archaeological  research looking at the future of  archaeology  and uh some film stuff in the works so  cool well thank you guys so much this  was fantastic and thank you all for  coming we really appreciate it thank you  for coming  [Applause]  thank you

